WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.092
A recursive query is easier to understand if you simulate it.

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:07.192
Iteration zero returns the anchor.

00:00:07.192 --> 00:00:10.527
The next iteration finds direct reports.

00:00:10.527 --> 00:00:14.352
The following iteration finds reports of those employees.

00:00:14.352 --> 00:00:18.582
When no new child rows match, recursion stops.

00:00:18.582 --> 00:00:22.497
This mental model helps you debug the join relationship.

00:00:22.497 --> 00:00:28.157
Connect this idea to a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions.

00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:34.027
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.027 --> 00:00:42.272
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.272 --> 00:00:48.427
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:48.427 --> 00:00:54.527
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
